{title: Your Way}
{artist: Larry Holder / Elton Smith}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: 80}

>Lyrics

Introduction

Verse 1

Lord, please bring us grace to face the things

We cannot understand.

The mysteries surround us

In this world of fallen man.

All along this life-long journey

We're dependent on Your love,

The mercy and the grace that

Comes from You alone, above...

Chorus

Be our comfort, be our shield.

Be our strength, Lord, as we yield

All our lives, Lord, every day

As Your Spirit draws us on

Out of night into the dawn

From the storm into the calm

Of Your Way.

Verse 2

We cast aside the petty things.

We know they matter least of all,

And reach out for Your loving arms

As on Your Name we call.

Searching for the Truth

That You have given to us in Your Word.

We gather here to praise You, now,

For You alone are Lord...

(Repeat Chorus)

Be our comfort, be our shield.

Be our strength, Lord, as we yield

All our lives, Lord, every day

As Your Spirit draws us on

Out of night into the dawn,

From the storm into the calm

Of Your Way,

Of Your Way,

Of Your Way.
